---
import styles from './ArchitecturalBet.module.scss';
---

<div class={styles.copy}>
  <p>
    At Frame Foundry I put every customer organisation in one shared Postgres database, with a
    tenant ID on every row. For a small team shipping weekly, one schema meant one set of
    migrations, one backup and one place to look when something broke. A database per tenant would
    have multiplied that work before we had the customers to justify it.
  </p>
  <p>
    The cost is that isolation depends on every query remembering its tenant filter, and one missed
    filter could show one organisation another's data. So once the data model settled, I rolled out
    row-level security. Now the database itself blocks access to other organisations' rows, and the
    filter in the application is the first check rather than the only one.
  </p>
</div>
